      "old": "Let \\(\\Gamma\\) be a finite union of positively oriented rectifiable Jordan curves enclosing the spectra of \\(A_f\\) and \\(A_c\\). If \\(g\\) is holomorphic on a neighborhood of the enclosed region, then",
      "new": "Let \\(\\Gamma\\) be the positively oriented rectifiable boundary of a finite union of pairwise disjoint bounded Jordan domains. Assume that both spectra lie inside this union and that \\(\\Gamma\\) lies in the common resolvent set. Thus its winding number is one about every spectral point. If \\(g\\) is holomorphic on a neighborhood of the closure of the union, then",
